    <bpmn:process id="W_W2555" name="W2555. Gray Market &amp; Unauthorized Channel Detection" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Anomalous scan patterns or market monitoring alerts
Frequency: Weekly monitoring; ad-hoc investigations
Volume: ~5–10 investigations/month
Owner: LP Analyst
Participants: LP Analyst, LP Manager, Category Manager, Legal
Source: workflow W2555 — Gray Market &amp; Unauthorized Channel Detection</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W2555_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W2555_Lane1" name="LP Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W2555_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W2555_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W2555_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W2555_Lane2" name="LP Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W2555_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W2555_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W2555_Start4" name="Anomalous scan patterns or market monitoring alerts">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W2555_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W2555_Task5" name="LP Analyst monitors for gray market indicators: BuildRight-serialized products…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: LP Analyst monitors for gray market indicators: BuildRight-serialized products found in unauthorized retail channels (online marketplaces, competitor stores), geographic scan anomalies (products scanning far from authorized store), bulk scan patterns (reseller activity detection)
Responsible (R): LP Analyst
Accountable (A): LP Manager
Duration: 2–3 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W2555_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W2555_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W2555_Task6" name="Analyst investigates suspicious patterns: traces product origin through serial…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Analyst investigates suspicious patterns: traces product origin through serial chain-of-custody, identifies purchase point (store/POS transaction), determines if diversion occurred at vendor, DC, or store level; compiles evidence dossier
Responsible (R): LP Analyst
Accountable (A): LP Manager
Duration: 1–2 days per case</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W2555_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W2555_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W2555_Task7" name="LP Manager escalates confirmed gray market cases: to Category Manager for…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: LP Manager escalates confirmed gray market cases: to Category Manager for vendor discussion (if vendor-side diversion), to Legal for contractual enforcement, to LP team for store-level investigation (if internal diversion); implements controls: quantity limits for high-risk products, enhanced tracking for repeat offenders
Responsible (R): LP Manager
Accountable (A): COO
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W2555_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W2555_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W2555_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W2555_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W2555_Annotation9">
